WIP / PoC: Support image digests in kolla_container.

An operator can pin a service to an exact image by giving its
<service>_image_full as a digest reference, repository@sha256:<hex>.
Podman pulls such an image, but the Docker worker cannot, and would not
recognise it once pulled:

* parse_image splits an image at its last colon, which falls inside the
  digest, so pull_image asked docker-py for the repository
  "repository@sha256" with the tag "<hex>". docker-py strips the
  "@sha256" and the daemon is asked for a tag named after the bare hex
  string, which does not exist.
* check_image only compares an image's RepoTags. With Docker's classic
  image store an image pulled by digest has no tags, only RepoDigests, so
  compare_image would report every such container as differing from its
  image, and it would be recreated on every run.

The Docker worker now splits a digest reference at the "@" and passes
the digest as the tag, which the Engine API accepts in place of one, and
looks a digest reference up in RepoDigests. A tag given alongside a
digest is dropped, as Docker ignores it. The shared parse_image is
unchanged, because podman-py rebuilds the reference by joining the
repository and tag with a colon, which is why Podman already worked.

get_image_id is unchanged: its images(name=...) filter matches a digest
reference with both the classic and the containerd image stores.

